# corpus.list — pinned parity case list (feature 050, US3 T037).
# Single source of truth for record_dart_goldens.sh (recorder) AND
# run_gleam_corpus.sh (comparator). See corpus-manifest.md for rationale.
#
# Record grammar (first token per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored):
#   block <id>            begin a runtime case (Section A). id is the golden stem.
#   file  <relpath>       a source file co-loaded for the current block (repeatable;
#                         Dart loads sequentially, Gleam loads them concatenated).
#   goal  <text>          a goal to run in the current block (repeatable; text is
#                         verbatim, incl. spaces/backslashes — read with `read -r`).
#   loadcase <section> <relpath>   a load-outcome case (sections B/C/D). The golden
#                         stem is derived from <relpath> (/=>__ , .glp stripped).
#   guardcase <id> <clause...>     an inline load-outcome case (section E); the
#                         remainder is a one-line .glp source written to a temp file.
#
# Paths are repo-relative (POSIX). The scripts resolve REPO_ROOT and apply the
# Windows-path conversion the Dart REPL needs (cygpath -m), same as run_all_tests.sh.

# =============================================================================
# SECTION A — runtime goal-outcome cases
# =============================================================================

